{%- comment -%}
  Renders one row per applied discount, covering BOTH cart-level applications and
  line-level allocations.

  Why both: an order-class discount (the 5% spend tier) lands in
  cart.cart_level_discount_applications, but a product-class one only ever appears
  inside each line's line_level_discount_allocations. The ₹300 / ₹700 spend tiers are
  deliberately product-class — that is what lets them stack with the 5% while still
  never stacking with each other — so a summary that loops only the cart-level list
  silently drops them, and a shopper at ₹3,000 sees the 5% but no sign of the ₹300.

  Line-level allocations arrive one per line, so they are summed by discount title to
  give a single row per discount rather than one per product.

  Accepts:
  - style: {String} 'badge' (default) draws the crimson chip used on the cart page;
      'ledger' draws a plain hairline row for the drawer's summary card. The
      grouping logic is identical either way — only the wrapper markup differs.

  Usage:
  {% render 'cart-savings-rows' %}
  {% render 'cart-savings-rows', style: 'ledger' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # Collect the distinct line-level discount titles. Liquid has no map, so the
  # delimiters make `contains` an exact-token test rather than a substring one.
  #
  # The delimiter is the three-character sentinel below, not a bare '|'. A merchant
  # is perfectly free to name a discount "Diwali | 10% Off", and a pipe delimiter
  # would split that title into two bogus tokens and corrupt the seen-list, giving
  # duplicated or merged savings rows.
  assign cs_sep = '|~|'
  assign cs_seen = cs_sep
  for cs_item in cart.items
    for cs_alloc in cs_item.line_level_discount_allocations
      assign cs_title = cs_alloc.discount_application.title
      assign cs_probe = cs_sep | append: cs_title | append: cs_sep
      unless cs_seen contains cs_probe
        assign cs_seen = cs_seen | append: cs_title | append: cs_sep
      endunless
    endfor
  endfor
  assign cs_titles = cs_seen | split: cs_sep

  assign cs_style = style | default: 'badge'
  comment
    Admin names these for the merchant — "₹300 Off — Spend ₹3000". In the drawer
    the qualifying half is noise twice over: the shopper has by definition already
    met it, and the ladder directly above states what is still to come. The cart
    PAGE keeps the full title, where the column is wide and the ladder is further
    away. Same shortening rule as line-discounts.liquid, so the two never disagree.
  endcomment
  if cs_style == 'ledger'
    assign cs_li = 'cart-summary__row cart-summary__row--off'
    assign cs_k = 'cart-summary__rk'
    assign cs_v = 'cart-summary__rv'
  else
    assign cs_li = 'cart-totals__savings-item'
    assign cs_k = 'cart-totals__label'
    assign cs_v = 'badge badge--onsale flex items-center gap-1d5 font-medium leading-none rounded-full'
  endif
-%}

{%- for discount in cart.cart_level_discount_applications -%}
  {%- if discount.total_allocated_amount > 0 -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign cs_label = discount.title
      if cs_style == 'ledger'
        assign cs_label = cs_label | split: '—' | first | split: '–' | first | split: ' - ' | first | strip
      endif
    -%}
    <li class="{{ cs_li }}">
      <span class="{{ cs_k }}">{%- render 'usd-inr-text', text: cs_label -%}</span>
      <span class="{{ cs_v }}">−{% render 'money-display', amount: discount.total_allocated_amount %}</span>
    </li>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- for cs_title in cs_titles -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign cs_title_size = cs_title | size
    assign cs_total = 0
    if cs_title_size > 0
      for cs_item in cart.items
        for cs_alloc in cs_item.line_level_discount_allocations
          if cs_alloc.discount_application.title == cs_title
            assign cs_total = cs_total | plus: cs_alloc.amount
          endif
        endfor
      endfor
    endif
  -%}
  {%- if cs_total > 0 -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign cs_label = cs_title
      if cs_style == 'ledger'
        assign cs_label = cs_label | split: '—' | first | split: '–' | first | split: ' - ' | first | strip
      endif
    -%}
    <li class="{{ cs_li }}">
      <span class="{{ cs_k }}">{%- render 'usd-inr-text', text: cs_label -%}</span>
      <span class="{{ cs_v }}">−{% render 'money-display', amount: cs_total %}</span>
    </li>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
